From d4a08e52f74480f8992bb2d1b35cac866a8d73b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:11:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix workbench / item building so the project compiles and
 runs on Godot 4.7.2

The workbench, item and bot code from the last update had never been run in
Godot. Opening the project failed with 12 GDScript parse errors ("Cannot infer
the type of ... because the value doesn't have a set type"), which also stopped
lobby_room.gd and everything depending on it from loading.

Parse fixes (explicit types on values read from untyped Dictionaries):
- bot_brain.gd: line telegraph end point, cone telegraph vector
- lobby_room.gd: party roster key list
- player.gd: _sync_move_mult
- enemy.gd: nearest-target distance, attack damage, forks end point,
  telegraph progress, line telegraph normal
- skills.gd: dash_zone destination

Workbench:
- WorkbenchUI now closes itself whenever the server would refuse shopping
  (LOADING, YARD, VICTORY, DEFEAT), instead of staying open with dead buttons.
- Replace stale 'crafting = TODO' comments on Player.item_flat/item_pct and in
  GAME_LOOP_DRAFT.md; list the item polish that is actually still open.

Verified headlessly on Godot 4.7.2: project imports with no errors; a real
3-player match (1 human + 2 bots) exercised buy / craft / auto-build, slot and
Ether limits, distance and phase gating, all 14 recipes, bot shopping, request
routing and the UI (60 checks pass); a sped-up soak through yard, prep, siege
and feast produced no engine errors.
---
 scripts/GAME_LOOP_DRAFT.md |  5 +++--
 scripts/bot_brain.gd       |  4 ++--
 scripts/enemy.gd           | 10 +++++-----
 scripts/lobby_room.gd      |  2 +-
 scripts/player.gd          |  6 +++---
 scripts/skills.gd          |  2 +-
 scripts/workbench_ui.gd    |  3 +++
 7 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/GAME_LOOP_DRAFT.md b/scripts/GAME_LOOP_DRAFT.md
index 9d6b0ab..09f2eb1 100644
--- a/scripts/GAME_LOOP_DRAFT.md
+++ b/scripts/GAME_LOOP_DRAFT.md
@@ -64,7 +64,7 @@ server spawns the 3 players and runs the loop.
  LOADING → for wave 1..5:
    YARD (60s)         spawn pests (cap 18); kill = Ether to ALL 3 wallets; death = auto-revive after 10s
    dinner bell        yard pests cleared, dead players revived (100%), everyone teleported to kitchen
-   KITCHEN_PREP (10s) workbench window (crafting UI = TODO)
+   KITCHEN_PREP (10s) workbench window: press F at the Workbench to buy Commons / craft Rares+Epics (also usable in SIEGE + FEAST)
    SIEGE              3 sub-waves; spawn vectors by difficulty (Normal: L | Hard: 2 rotating | Hell: all 3)
                       sub-wave 3 adds the miniboss; dead players stay dead until it dies (revive @50%)
                       wave 5: after miniboss → Trash King (phase 2 at 50%: leaps on table, eats food)
@@ -107,7 +107,8 @@ each attack kind draws its own red/yellow indicator (line, circle, cone) on all
 7. Skills that need persistent objects (Snap's tripwire) are approximated as a one-shot line.
 
 ## 10. Not yet built (next steps)
-Workbench/shop UI + item crafting (stat hooks exist: `Player.item_flat / item_pct`), 3 passives + emblem
+Item polish (Workbench itself is done): Cockroach Spray / Zapper wide-cone art, Turbo Vacuum Boots phasing
+(needs collisions), Fridge-door aura slowing enemy attack speed. Also: 3 passives + emblem
 loadout (`on_basic_attack` hook in `srv_attack`), lobby passive/emblem icons, Spirit Crumb spectator ping,
 procedural yard, real sprites/animations + collision shapes, save system for levels/currencies/gacha,
 energy + backend payout, skill-cooldown HUD.
diff --git a/scripts/bot_brain.gd b/scripts/bot_brain.gd
index bb9a2aa..671850d 100644
--- a/scripts/bot_brain.gd
+++ b/scripts/bot_brain.gd
@@ -130,12 +130,12 @@ func _dodge(p: Player) -> Vector2:
 			"line":
 				var d := Vector2.from_angle(t.angle)
 				var a: Vector2 = t.pos
-				var b := a + d * t.a
+				var b: Vector2 = a + d * float(t.a)
 				if Combat.seg_dist(pos, a, b) < t.b * 0.5 + 35.0:
 					var side := d.orthogonal()
 					return side if (pos - a).dot(side) >= 0.0 else -side
 			"cone":
-				var to := pos - t.pos
+				var to: Vector2 = pos - t.pos
 				if to.length() < t.a + 30.0 and absf(Vector2.from_angle(t.angle).angle_to(to)) < deg_to_rad(t.b * 0.5) + 0.3:
 					return to.normalized()
 	return Vector2.ZERO
